infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Four cold-start levers, cheapest first — each cuts a different phase
  desc Profile first, then match the lever to the dominant phase; pick the wrong one and you get nothing
  lists
    - label Lazy require — skip a rare-path dep
      desc require() the heavy dep inside the function that uses it, so a path most invocations never take loads nothing at boot. Catch — it defers, not removes: a common-path dep still pays the same resolution + compile, just on first call.
    - label Bundle (esbuild / ncc) — kill resolution I/O
      desc Inlines the whole graph into one file, so the loader does one stat()+read() instead of tens of thousands — a Lambda fell from ~3s to under 1s. Catch — no help for eval, and you must tree-shake dead deps to hold the win.
    - label NODE_COMPILE_CACHE — reuse warm bytecode
      desc Serializes V8 bytecode keyed by source, so warm boots skip parse+compile — the 20-40% compile slice can drop by an order of magnitude. Catch — the first run pays full cost to populate it, and serverless needs a persistent cache dir, not /tmp.
    - label Startup snapshot — freeze the post-init heap
      desc --build-snapshot runs init once and captures the V8 heap; --snapshot-blob restores it instantly, skipping eval entirely. Catch — no open handles at snapshot time, an experimental API, and the blob is locked to the exact Node version.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
